Falsifies `system_tests::user::std_tests::a_std_program_gives_back_every_frame_it_was_given`.

Architecture: aarch64

The defect: one page of a std spawn's wiring comes from the kernel's own frames again instead of
the region the holding reclaims, here the configuration page, which is where this leak lived until
2026-10-10 (UTC) with the stack and the clock service. Nothing faults and every transcript still
passes; the page is simply never returned.

Expected to fail: the free count after the second spawn is one frame short. Measured 2026-10-10
(UTC) on aarch64: red with "a std spawn kept 1 frames after it was handed back".

